Does this also work on macOS

No, this specific in-memory execution technique does not work on macOS.

The combination of memfd_create and /proc/self/fd/ relies on Linux-specific kernel features.
Why It Fails on macOS

    No memfd_create: macOS (Darwin kernel) does not implement the memfd_create syscall for creating anonymous in-memory files.

    No /proc Filesystem: macOS does not mount a /proc pseudo-filesystem, so /proc/self/fd/N paths do not exist.

    Code Signing & Hardened Runtime: macOS requires binaries to exist on disk as signed files to execute. The OS kernel actively blocks executing arbitrary memory regions directly as standalone processes.

How to Handle macOS

If you need cross-platform support in your Rust project, use conditional compilation (#[cfg(target_os = "...")]):

    Linux: Use the in-memory memfd_create approach.

    macOS: Write the embedded bytes to a temporary file (e.g., via the tempfile crate), grant execution permissions, spawn the process, and let it clean itself up when finished.

Cross-Platform Rust Implementation
Rust

use std::fs::File;
use std::io::Write;
use std::process::{Child, Command};

static SHIM_BYTES: &[u8] = include_bytes!(concat!(env!("OUT_DIR"), "/shim_embedded"));

#[cfg(target_os = "linux")]
fn spawn_shim() -> std::io::Result<Child> {
    use std::os::fd::AsRawFd;

    let memfd_name = std::ffi::CString::new("shim_process").unwrap();
    let raw_fd = unsafe { libc::memfd_create(memfd_name.as_ptr(), libc::MFD_CLOEXEC) };
    if raw_fd < 0 {
        return Err(std::io::Error::last_os_error());
    }

    let mut mem_file = unsafe { File::from_raw_fd(raw_fd) };
    mem_file.write_all(SHIM_BYTES)?;

    Command::new(format!("/proc/self/fd/{}", raw_fd)).spawn()
}

#[cfg(target_os = "macos")]
fn spawn_shim() -> std::io::Result<Child> {
    use std::os::unix::fs::PermissionsExt;

    // Create a temporary file on macOS
    let temp_dir = std::env::temp_dir();
    let shim_path = temp_dir.join(format!("shim_tmp_{}", std::process::id()));

    let mut file = File::create(&shim_path)?;
    file.write_all(SHIM_BYTES)?;

    // Grant execute permissions (chmod +x)
    let mut perms = file.metadata()?.permissions();
    perms.set_mode(0o700);
    file.set_permissions(perms)?;

    // Spawn the temporary binary
    let child = Command::new(&shim_path).spawn();

    // Clean up temporary file path from disk after spawning
    let _ = std::fs::remove_file(shim_path);

    child
}

